{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333655-new-gm-troubles","id":1333655,"title":"New GM troubles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-02T05:33:05-07:00","id":1333655,"title":"New GM troubles","content":"I'm new into CoD and I have a bit difficult players: they want to have a vampire/werewolf campaign where 2 players will be vampires and three will be werewolves. I would like them to have equal fun, but I have in mind the following questions:<br /> <br /> 1. I don't get entirely how Uratha kills a spirit. They shred it apart or should they do something more to get rid of it for good? Only with his claws and teeth?<br /> 2. What can hurt a spirit? I know that vampires in my campaign should have any means of defending themselves.<br /> 3. From a mechanical standpoint: how do you balance enemies to be not too powerful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25610-penny","user":"Penny","date":". 09-02-2019, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25610-penny","name":"Penny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T09:24:03-07:00","id":1333685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333655-new-gm-troubles#post1333655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I don't get entirely how Uratha kills a spirit. They shred it apart or should they do something more to get rid of it for good? Only with his claws and teeth?</div> </div> </div> </div>A spirit is destroyed for good if it loses all of its Corpus to lethal or aggravated damage while it has no Essence left in its system.<br /> <br /> The &quot;easiest&quot; way to accomplish this is by using its Bane to cause aggravated damage, which costs the spirit a point of Essence per box of aggravated damage it takes, but more powerful spirits have banes that are necessarily harder to acquire or leverage.<br /> <br /> The more reliable means of destroying a spirit in this fashion is for werewolves with the Sacred Hunt rite's <i>Siskur-Dah</i> Condition to bring down the spirit, at which point they can split its leftover Essence between them as they like, including taking all of it and then striking the finishing blow; doing so typically nudges their Harmony toward Spirit, but it's a method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. What can hurt a spirit? I know that vampires in my campaign should have any means of defending themselves. </div> </div> </div>Every spirit has a Bane that causes them harm, frays their Manifestations, and acts as a solid barrier against their intrusion; Materialized spirits are also vulnerable to physical assault, albeit with the same considerations as vampires receive vis-a-vis weapons and their relative use in harming living systems the target does not possess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T10:02:58-07:00","id":1333691,"title":"","content":"<b>The Pack </b>addresses how Vampires might integrate a werewolf pack too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T10:08:29-07:00","id":1333695,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that, while not their forte, vampires aren't completely unarmed for handling spirits, albeit not as well as werewolves or various Shadow-inclined entities obviously. The Circle of the Crone's magic plays well with options in that field, it's not unreasonable to think that the Lancea Et Sanctum and Ordo Dracul don't have their own tools, and there's a lot of weird nooks and crannies in the realm of what the Blood can do that a serious seeker can often emerge drenched in crimson from the depths with a tool for the occasion.<br /> <br /> It's often a matter of deep lore diving and hard prices paid, but if your vampires are ever caught in a hard period of time without their werewolves, the Curses have their teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T15:37:41-07:00","id":1333756,"title":"","content":"Thank you for answers. I have another question: if Spirit-Ridden human is slain does spirit take any damage? Or any damage done to the mount is affecting Corpus of the spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25610-penny","name":"Penny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T16:08:36-07:00","id":1333759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333655-new-gm-troubles?p=1333756#post1333756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for answers. I have another question: if Spirit-Ridden human is slain does spirit take any damage? Or any damage done to the mount is affecting Corpus of the spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typical Claimed eject their core spirit upon death or destruction and no special note is made of their taking damage; this largely tracks with the similar but distinct process of possession by the Embodiment of a Strix, where the only way an Owl takes a hit to its Corpus from its host's destruction is if the killing blow involved increasingly massive amounts of damage, and that's for entities that aren't naturally out-of-phase with material reality.<br /> <br /> Plain old Urged and Possessed likewise apply no carry-over damage upon death, but the host making contact with the spirit's bane causes the spirit damage just as it would if it weren't attached to a body, though the damage they take then is lethal instead of aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T13:03:01-07:00","id":1334010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333655-new-gm-troubles?p=1333685#post1333685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;easiest&quot; way to accomplish this is by using its Bane to cause aggravated damage, which costs the spirit a point of Essence per box of aggravated damage it takes</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't find such information in handbook, so from where it come from?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25610-penny","name":"Penny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T14:01:38-07:00","id":1334020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333655-new-gm-troubles?p=1334010#post1334010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't find such information in handbook, so from where it come from?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> P186, 'Spirits record and heal from wounds the same way as human characters, but in addition lose one point of Essence for every aggravated wound they suffer.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-05T00:24:12-07:00","id":1334050,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I must have skipped it during my search. There is one thing that bothers me. When you beat something long enough (even applying only bashing damage) you start inflicting aggravated wounds. Does this rule apply to spirits or they always explode and go dormant? Does spirit have to roll for Resistance when it fills all boxes with bashing damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25610-penny","name":"Penny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-05T03:11:52-07:00","id":1334060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333655-new-gm-troubles?p=1334050#post1334050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, I must have skipped it during my search. There is one thing that bothers me. When you beat something long enough (even applying only bashing damage) you start inflicting aggravated wounds. Does this rule apply to spirits or they always explode and go dormant? Does spirit have to roll for Resistance when it fills all boxes with bashing damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Entities that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated wounds explode into a burst of ephemera or Mana stylized to their natures.&quot;<br /> (Edit: Copied from Mage, hence the reference to Mana, but applies to all games.)<br /> <br /> Once you've dealt full lethal the spirit discorporates, so the only aggravated damage dealt from rollover would be excess damage in the strike that took it to full lethal.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't have wound penalties and no mechanics associated with taking full bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}